 {"id": "BT-032", "title": "validate silently passes a corrupt fixtures.jsonl: validateFixtures drops IterParsed's error", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "Found by QA-BOARDCTL-001 tick 83 while building real corruption coverage: with ONLY fixtures.jsonl corrupted (first row truncated mid-JSON), boardctl validate reports '0 fixtures' and RESULT: OK exit 0. validateFixtures (internal/board/validate.go:307) calls IterParsed but never captures its returned error; the following if err != nil re-checks the outer ReadJSONLLines error (nil at that point). validateTasks/validateEvents both capture ierr := IterParsed(...) and report it. Silent-pass in a validation tool leaks fixture rows into ordinary task reads with no operator signal.", "created_at": "2026-09-17 08:02:17", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "f2bee5c", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "validateFixtures now captures IterParsed's error (internal/board/validate.go:315 ierr :=, :328 if ierr != nil -> rep.Add error naming fixtures.jsonl), matching validateTasks/validateEvents. Previously the outer ReadJSONLLines error was re-checked instead (nil at that point), so a truncated fixtures.jsonl produced no finding and validate exited 0. Regression: the fixtures_jsonl_truncated_row subtest is back in the TestQACorruption table (real run() on t.TempDir board, single-file mutation, exit 1 + target file named + RESULT: FAIL, zero-write hash proof, restore-to-clean) and is RED-proven load-bearing. Foreman live probe on a scratch board: corrupted fixtures -> '[error] fixtures.jsonl: line 1: unexpected EOF' + RESULT: FAIL exit 1; restored -> RESULT: OK exit 0. Docs gap section updated to FIXED.", "complexity": 2, "updated_at": "2026-09-17 08:10:39", "foreman_note": "Judge PASS verdict dir .gitreins/history/2026-09-17/778a484a (the PRINTED id eea33170 is not the on-disk dir). Worker glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm session 20260917_030230_1e5b3b, ~9 min. Commit f2bee5c pushed, 0 unpushed, CI run 08:08Z success. Foreman verified the diff and ran an independent live probe (corrupt -> FAIL exit 1, restore -> OK exit 0).", "completed_at": "2026-09-17 03:10:00", "depends_on": [], "review_notes": null}
 {"id": "BT-033", "title": "toolchain vuln + no gate: go.mod pins go 1.26 (resolves to vulnerable go1.26.5), govulncheck finds 3 REACHABLE stdlib vulns (net/http reached by serve, crypto/tls, encoding/asn1 via render) and nothing in the repo gates them; bump go 1.26 -> 1.26.6 and add the vuln gate (make vuln-check + CI + test)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "Tick 84 discovery. govulncheck ./... exits 3 at HEAD 711ea63 with 3 reachable stdlib vulns, all 'Fixed in go1.26.6': GO-2026-6089 net/http (cmd/boardctl/serve.go:125 http.Server.Serve), GO-2026-6090 crypto/tls (serve + render/report.go:76), GO-2026-5972 encoding/asn1 (render/report.go:76). CERTAIN: 'go list -m -u all' is clean, so this is stdlib, not a dep. The fix recipe is PRE-VERIFIED in the off-by-one corpus (class go-toolchain-stdlib-vuln-upgrade, answer 1212, status verified): bump the go directive, GOTOOLCHAIN=auto downloads the patched toolchain, no source change. The second half is the ungated half: no govulncheck anywhere in Makefile/CI, which is why this rotted unnoticed.", "created_at": "2026-09-18 02:37:20", "capability_tags": ["go", "ci", "security", "makefile"], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "08655c4b4cb386ab2275856f8f699aef80d1e1c1", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "go.mod now declares 'go 1.26.6' (was 'go 1.26' resolving to the vulnerable go1.26.5 toolchain): govulncheck ./... went from exit 3 with 3 REACHABLE stdlib advisories (GO-2026-6089 net/http reached by serve, GO-2026-6090 crypto/tls, GO-2026-5972 encoding/asn1) to exit 0 'No vulnerabilities found.'. New check-only internal/vulncheck package gates it on three surfaces: make vuln-check, the CI 'Vulnerability-check' step behind a pinned govulncheck v1.7.0 install, and plain go test ./... . Foreman-verified load-bearing: pointing $GOVULNCHECK at a fake exit-3 scanner makes TestVulncheck FAIL (exit 1).", "complexity": 3, "updated_at": "2026-09-18 02:48:14", "foreman_note": "Tick 84 discovery finding. Fix recipe came from the pre-solve corpus (class go-toolchain-stdlib-vuln-upgrade, answer 1212, verified) rather than being re-derived. Judge PASS, verdict .gitreins/history/2026-09-18/02daf294/verdict.json (printed id dada899b again not the dir). CI run 35300520344 success with both new steps visible in gh run view. Companion row BT-034 cut in the same tick because the published v0.1.4 bytes still shipped the vulnerable toolchain.", "completed_at": "2026-09-17 21:48:14", "depends_on": [], "review_notes": null}
