pping shell bug fixed; dedupe-board documented source-only.", "foreman_note": "Judge PASS .gitreins/history/2026-09-19/0234fab1/verdict.json (printed id 8921e53f). Identity chain: asset vcs.revision 9f437bc == git rev-parse v0.1.6^{commit} == origin/main. v0.1.5 asset vcs.revision f9b4041 = the drift premise. Gates fresh: build, vet, test -short, fmt-check, version-check, vuln-check. CI green: 35435108890, 35435109427, 35435110524. Residual noted for a follow-up if wanted: cmd/dedupe-board still has no test files.", "completed_at": "2026-09-19 04:35:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "fa7146fa6faa8225a7de74e1d95d50df26e3dc239e95b75af44e18ae20c9a12a"}}
 {"id": "BT-037", "title": "header --set-* on a HEADERLESS board writes header counters INTO the first task row (bit: 9 keys -> 10 on CHT-001)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-19 while adding the worktree/branch/sessions fields.\n\nREPRO (on a copy, never the live board):\n  1. board with tasks.jsonl + events.jsonl and NO board.jsonl (real case: /home/kara/coding-hermes-tools/.coding-hermes/board/).\n  2. `boardctl -C <board> header --set-ticks-total 90`\n  3. prints: header updated (line 1 of tasks.jsonl): ticks_total, updated_at\n  4. RESULT: task CHT-001 (the FIRST task row) grew from 9 keys to 10 -- it now carries ticks_total:90 and a rewritten updated_at. A real task row was silently mutated by a header operation.\n\nROOT CAUSE: with no board.jsonl the topology detection falls back to 'header = line 1 of tasks.jsonl' and never checks that line 1 is header-SHAPED. Line 1 here is an ordinary task row (id/title/status), so the write lands in a task.\n\nSAME ROOT CAUSE, second symptom: `boardctl validate` on that board reports 3 false errors -- 'tasks.jsonl header: version / ticks_total / ticks_idle is not an integer counter' -- because it validates a task row as a header.\n\nIMPACT: the tool whose entire contract is byte-preserving surgery on non-target rows silently rewrites one. Any headerless board in the fleet is one `header --set-*` away from a corrupted first row.\n\nFIX SHAPE: when board.jsonl is absent, or line 1 carries task keys (id/title/status), classify the board HEADERLESS: (a) `header --set-*` must refuse with an explicit 'no header on this board' error instead of writing; (b) `validate` reports an informational 'headerless board (no board.jsonl)' line rather than integer-counter errors; (c) hard guard -- never write a header key into a row that also carries id/title/status. Tests: a headerless fixture for both paths, plus a RED proof that the guard fires.", "created_at": "2026-09-19 13:50:04", "updated_at": "2026-09-19 14:35:26", "capability_tags": ["board", "integrity", "corruption"], "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "5f5a799f42cbc349609a8b2a71097659da65d3e1", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "header --set-* now refuses on headerless boards (no board.jsonl AND line 1 not header-shaped) with an explicit 'no header on this board' error (ErrNoHeader); validate/doctor emit one informational headerless line and skip the false integer-counter errors; rowIsTaskShape hard guard blocks header keys in any id/title/status row. 17 new tests (bt037_headerless_test.go x10, bt037_headerless_cli_test.go x7), RED-proven by disabling the guards (12 failures with the exact pre-fix symptoms). Foreman live probe on a copy of the real coding-hermes-tools board: header --set-ticks-total 90 -> exit 1, tasks.jsonl sha256 byte-identical, CHT-001 still 9 keys; validate exit 0 with zero false counter errors.", "foreman_note": "Tick 87. Judge PASS tier1+tier2, verdict .gitreins/history/2026-09-19/3a7c8352/verdict.json (printed id ab2be530 differs, as usual). CI green on both workflows for 5f5a799.", "completed_at": "2026-09-19 09:45:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b26be3d5fc0c877d12ad1da424178323b98c0de38c13d186535114919f4f84b7"}}
 {"id": "BT-038", "title": "DEPLOY: the installed boardctl (~/.local/bin, 2026-09-11) predates the BT-037 corruption fix -- the fix is merged+green but NOT live", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "FOUND 2026-09-19 while auditing a sibling repo's board (so: incidental, but real).\n\nMEASURED:\n  - deployed binary: ~/.local/bin/boardctl, mtime 2026-09-11 08:17\n  - BT-037 fix (5f5a799) commit date: 2026-09-19 09:28:54 -0500\n  => the installed tool still has the headerless-board corruption bug that BT-037 cured. Running the deployed\n     binary against a headerless board still reports 3 false integer-counter errors AND `header --set-*` still\n     writes header counters into the first task row.\n\nEVIDENCE (both binaries, same repo, same minute):\n    ~/.local/bin/boardctl -C . validate      -> RESULT: FAIL (3 error(s), 5 warning(s))\n    <repo>/bin/boardctl   -C . validate      -> RESULT: OK (4 warning(s))   [informational 'headerless board' line]\n\nMITIGATION IN PLACE, so this is P2 not P1: the boardctl-foreman-ops skill instructs foremen to use the\nrepo-local ./bin/boardctl (4 references), which IS freshly built -- so live board writes are already using the\nfixed code. The stale copy is a convenience install that has drifted.\n\nWHAT TO DECIDE/SHIP:\n  1. a defined deploy step so ~/.local/bin/boardctl is refreshed when boardctl merges (today it is manual and\n     therefore silently stale);\n  2. `boardctl version` should be enough to detect this -- if it does not name the commit, it cannot;\n  3. do the refresh under the drain law (do NOT swap the binary while ticks are running -- 2 ticks were live\n     when this was found).", "created_at": "2026-09-19 15:25:17", "updated_at": "2026-09-20 05:38:18", "capability_tags": ["deploy", "install", "stale"], "complexity": 1, "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "153e141", "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": "rebuilt+installed ~/.local/bin/boardctl from