 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-10", "title": "ID-recycled near-dupes: 6+ live boards carry many DISTINCT findings filed under ONE recycled id (asce QA-ASCE-1 x6) — validate flags the dupes and dedupe-board correctly refuses to collapse them, but no lane tool fixes the hygiene", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-09-22 (dogfood run, dedupe-board dry-run on live boards).\nEVIDENCE: asce board: id QA-ASCE-1 appears on 6 lines (97/105/112/118/119/124), each a DIFFERENT finding (different title AND reasoning: header-frozen, spawn-pool exhausted, port-range exhausted x2, bunker-dropped). Same pattern on ai_plays_poke (QA-AI-PLAYS-POKE-1..3 x4+), hivemind-work, dexdat-memory, speclang. dedupe-board dry-run on asce: groups=[] — CORRECT per the fingerprint definition (sha over normalized title+reasoning, which all differ), so the SG-126 one-shot is not the tool for this; but validate permanently errors (exit 1) on every such board and nothing else addresses it.\nROOT CAUSE: QA lanes re-used a fresh cycle-number instead of advancing the id (QA-ASCE-1, -2, -3 refiled every cycle).\nFIX DIRECTION: (a) lanes must always mint fresh ids (id-recycled = new finding under an old key); (b) boardctl: doctor already itemizes them — add an id-aware dedupe mode (keep earliest line per id, close later lines as superseded-by-earliest with their text preserved in the event log) OR a doctor --json machine output lanes can consume; (c) optionally: accept known-alias statuses (dispatched, closed) as read aliases so parked-heavy boards validate clean once ids are fixed.", "created_at": "2026-09-22T13:58:05Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-28T01:10:35Z", "worker_status": "complete", "detail": {"fingerprint": "9a02e51a7b1cea82be27d619c1a62105b2bde603d9d08d2d606aec0e2beada91"}, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "foreman_note": "Wave tick boardctl-2026-09-27-23-52-37; judge PASS verdict .gitreins/history/2026-09-28/910fbfbd (printed id 12cf32cf is not the dir). Fix direction (c) read-alias widening intentionally skipped per row (optional).", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/coding-hermes-boardctl-DF-BOARDCTL-10", "branch": "wt/DF-BOARDCTL-10", "commit_hash": "1ff31cc", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Id-aware dedupe shipped (worker 1ff31cc, merged d7aaeee): dedupe-board --by-id keeps the earliest row per id and closes later ones as superseded with original text preserved in the event log; dry-run proven inert by hash snapshot; asce-shaped 6-row recycled-id fixture + mixed + idempotency + CLI-level tests retire the cmd/dedupe-board [no test files] residual; fresh-id rule documented in help.", "sessions": ["20260927_191143_e86a02"], "completed_at": "2026-09-28T01:10:35Z", "capability_tags": []}
