 {"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-23", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "title": "vulncheck version pin skips a binary whose -version output has no parsable 'Scanner:' line — a stub or reimplementation defeats the pin by staying silent", "reasoning": "Run-18 boundary probe on wt/BT-064's fix (9393ed0): CheckVersion correctly refuses a parseable wrong version ('Scanner: govulncheck@v0.0.9' -> gate FAIL rc=2 naming expected v1.7.0 / actual v0.0.9), but a stub that prints a version banner WITHOUT the exact 'Scanner: govulncheck@' prefix is treated as absent and the gate proceeds green (proven: a stub echoing 'govulncheck@v0.0.9' makes make vuln-check rc=0). The skip is deliberate and documented in CheckVersion's doc comment ('PATH-fallback behavior unchanged'), and real govulncheck prints the line, so the practical risk is wrappers/reimplementations — but refusing exactly those is the pin's point. Fix direction: when the binary exists and -version exits 0 yet yields no Scanner line, at least WARN (or fail behind an explicit override env) instead of silently passing.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "2c46b72e95b8cdeeba93737e572fc69eb613dc4bf83ea113735088ece41e5c3d"}, "created_at": "2026-09-29T10:29:36Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "8671d10", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": null, "capability_tags": ["gates", "supply-chain"], "complexity": 2, "updated_at": "2026-09-29T11:20:00Z", "worker_summary": "merged to main beeabbc; tier-2 verdict PASS; worktree reaped", "foreman_note": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-29T11:35:00Z", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null}
 {"id": "REVIEW-BOARDCTL-011", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "title": "README documents validate --skip-bad-lines but not --repair — the SKIPPED-LINES error message sends users to an undocumented command", "reasoning": "Run-18: the repair path (daf0f3f, shipped in v0.1.8+) works exactly as specced — proven on synthetic damage (8 salvaged / 4 dropped with line numbers, tasks.jsonl byte-identical before/after, the rewritten file validates clean after a swap) and again on a fresh bunker box with the published v0.1.9 binary. But the README's validate section documents only --skip-bad-lines; --repair, tasks.rewritten.jsonl, and the diff-verify-then-swap workflow appear nowhere in README.md (discoverable only via validate --help or the commit message). A user whose first contact is the SKIPPED-LINES error ('salvage with boardctl validate --repair') finds no README backing for the command it names. Fix direction: add a short block after the --skip-bad-lines bullet: what --repair writes, that tasks.jsonl is never modified, and the manual-review-then-swap procedure.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "82005b1cedde13fba81f115476d71d7daccc39a2164edb58d06b2e31cd8a22e3"}, "created_at": "2026-09-29T10:29:36Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "4cf494a", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": null, "capability_tags": ["docs"], "complexity": 1, "updated_at": "2026-09-29T11:20:00Z", "worker_summary": "merged to main beeabbc; tier-2 verdict PASS; worktree reaped", "foreman_note": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-29T11:35:00Z", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null}
-{"id": "BT-070", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "title": "boardctl priority vocabulary is P0..P3 — extend it to P0..P5 (Bane 2026-09-30)", "reasoning": "BANE 2026-09-30 (verbatim): \"boardctl needs a task added to it that it supports upto P5.\"\n\nToday the canonical on-disk priority vocabulary is {P0,P1,P2,P3}:\n- internal/board/validate.go:168 — the BT-048 PriorityVocabulary map + the \"not in vocabulary {P0,P1,P2,P3}\" warning text (lines 180/183).\n- internal/board/validate.go:392 — `titlePriorityToken = regexp.MustCompile(`(^|[^A-Za-z0-9])([Pp][0-3])([^A-Za-z0-9]|$)`)` (title-vs-field drift detection is P0-P3 only).\n- NormalizePriority — accepts bare `0`..`3` (and case variants) → canonical Pn.\n- internal/render/load.go:480 + internal/render/template.go:812 — `priorityLabel` documents the read-side rule as \"string form as-is (P0..P3)\".\n- create/update `--priority` flag validates against the same set.\n\nExtend the vocabulary to {P0..P5}.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. `boardctl create|update --priority P4` and `--priority P5` are accepted; P0..P3 behaviour unchanged.\n2. Validation treats P4/P5 as in-vocabulary; the warning/error text naming the set reads {P0..P5}.\n3. NormalizePriority maps bare `4`/`5` → P4/P5 (mirrors the 0-3 rule).\n4. `titlePriorityToken` matches P0..P5, so title-carries-Pn/field-mismatch drift is caught for P4/P5 too.\n5. The render label + any ordering/rank map is TOTAL across P0..P5 (P4/P5 sort AFTER P3 in every list/queue view).\n6. Tests for each of 1-5; help text updated.\n\nWHY: the paperwork satellites (see the companion task) need P4/P5 to sit at the end of the queue — and the tool must accept the value before any lane can carry it.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "90b03dce768adedfd8ac7d401ac5581bce281ba74475dd0cae156d84399de646"}, "created_at": "2026-10-01T00:34:05Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "bf46263", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "PASS", "capability_tags": ["boardctl", "priority", "vocabulary", "validate"], "complexity": 3, "updated_at": "2026-10-01T00:34:05Z", "worker_summary": "Priority vocabulary extended P0..P3 -> P0..P5: PriorityVocabulary+NormalizePriority (read.go), validate set-text + titlePriorityToken [0-5], write/update/import error texts, render label docs, help text; P4/P5 tests + render-order test; go build/vet/test green; tier-2 judge PASS (e438ec77)", "foreman_note": "worker (glm-5.3-flash) implemented; foreman verified gate + push (origin/main..HEAD=0); CI green on main for bf46263", "completed_at": "2026-10-01T05:20:33", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null}
-{"id": "BT-071", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "title": "Paperwork lanes (docs/readme/review) file at P4/P5 so they always sort to the end (Bane 2026-09-30)", "reasoning": "BANE 2026-09-30 (verbatim): \"we also need to make sure the docs/readme/etc the ones that are just doing paperwork that they have a P4 or P5 so that they are always near the end.\"\n\nRows written by the paperwork satellites — docs, readme, review (the report-writers, whose deliverable is prose/a page, not code) — should resolve to P4 or P5 so they sort to the END in every board view and in the scheduler's pick order. They are real work, but they are never more urgent than the build/QA/PM rows above them, and today they crowd the top of the queue at P2/P3.\n\nDepends on the companion task (priority vocabulary P0..P5) — the tool must accept P4/P5 first.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. The row-writing path (boardctl `create`, and whatever helper the foremen use) DEFAULTS the priority to **P5** for a lane whose name ends in `-docs`, `-readme`, or `-review`, when no explicit `--priority` is given. (If a two-tier split is wanted, `-review` → P4 and `-docs`/`-readme` → P5; decide and document — the point is: never above P3.)\n2. An explicit `--priority` on the row OVERRIDES the default (a human can always promote a specific doc row).\n3. The rule keys on the lane-CLASS suffix, not a hardcoded per-repo or per-name list (matches how the scheduler derives lane classes).\n4. Documented in the boardctl docs; a test proves `create` for a `-docs`/`-readme`/`-review` lane with no `--priority` lands P5.\n5. Existing rows on live boards are NOT mass-rewritten by this change (it is a default for NEW writes); a separate sweep can re-prioritize the standing paperwork rows if wanted.\n\nOPEN QUESTION (state the answer in the row): does `-pm` (and `-sync`?) count as \"paperwork\"? Bane named docs/readme; the boundary should be explicit, not assumed.\n\nWHY: keeps the queue honest — the lanes whose output is a page never outrank the lanes whose output is a fix.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "5e6b41e93ca8ef9d94cf33b73bcd0fff4bea12fb8c39725cec88fefb03d60ec0"}, "created_at": "2026-10-01T00:34:05Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "505dd6a4e3a7a512e3f49f09697a18a7bb833fe1", "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "capability_tags": ["boardctl", "priority", "paperwork", "default"], "complexity": 2, "updated_at": "2026-10-01T06:49:09Z", "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": "BT-071 complete (505dd6a): create-side paperwork-lane default — lane suffix -review -> P4, -docs/-readme -> P5, everything else (primary/-qa/-pm/-sync) keeps P2; explicit --priority wins; update never invents a default so existing rows untouched. Rule keys on Board.LaneName() lane-class suffix (same identity the scheduler uses). RED-proven by mutation; go test ./... green; tier-1 guard PASS (full); 9-probe live battery green; pushed origin main.", "completed_at": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "depends_on": ["BT-070"]}
