nes whose output is a fix.", "detail": {"fingerprint": "5e6b41e93ca8ef9d94cf33b73bcd0fff4bea12fb8c39725cec88fefb03d60ec0"}, "created_at": "2026-10-01T00:34:05Z", "created_by": null, "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "505dd6a4e3a7a512e3f49f09697a18a7bb833fe1", "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "capability_tags": ["boardctl", "priority", "paperwork", "default"], "complexity": 2, "updated_at": "2026-10-03T15:39:23Z", "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": "BT-071 complete (505dd6a): create-side paperwork-lane default — lane suffix -review -> P4, -docs/-readme -> P5, everything else (primary/-qa/-pm/-sync) keeps P2; explicit --priority wins; update never invents a default so existing rows untouched. Rule keys on Board.LaneName() lane-class suffix (same identity the scheduler uses). RED-proven by mutation; go test ./... green; tier-1 guard PASS (full); 9-probe live battery green; pushed origin main.", "completed_at": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "depends_on": ["BT-070"]}
 {"id": "QA-BOARDCTL-2", "title": "QA ci-pass DIVERGENCE: act reproduces the CI workflow fresh and the Test step FAILS while the native suite passes (battery 2026-10-01)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "QA foreman cycle 2026-10-01 - fresh-system CI pass + chaos on hermes4friends (cell ci-pass). The repo's own GitHub workflow ran under act on a clean bunker agent and the Test step failed (rc=1) after Vet/Gofmt/Version-check/Spec-check/govulncheck all passed; the native go suite on the same tree PASSED. One of the two is lying about the repo's health: either the workflow carries an environment dependency the fresh container does not satisfy (a false CI-pass locally), or the native suite masks a failure the CI environment exposes. Which step assertion fails inside Test is visible in the evidence log.", "created_at": "2026-10-01 12:26:05", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "complexity": null, "updated_at": "2026-10-01 12:26:05", "foreman_note": "ROOT CAUSE (proven locally, act 0.2.89): TestBT053FleetFailureClassAndExit injects its failure via chmod 0500 (EACCES) on a hooks dir; act's node docker image runs as ROOT, which bypasses permission bits (CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE), so the write succeeds, no repo FAILs, and the test's 'must exit nonzero' assertion fails. Native suite runs as uid 1000 -> passes. Fresh-clone native run also passes => env-only divergence, not a repo defect; the workflow is healthy. FIX: euid==0 loud t.Skip with the reason. Verified: act reproduces the FAIL before fix; test passes natively; commit ac15ca8.", "completed_at": "2026-10-01", "depends_on": [], "review_notes": "EVIDENCE /tmp/qa-20261001-boardctl.jsonl cell=ci-pass: 'act failed (rc=1: ... Success - Main Vulnerability-check ... FAIL - Main Test [11.04s]) - native suite PASS'. REPRO: BUNKER_QA_SERVER=hermes4friends BUNKER_QA_HOST_KEY=~/.ssh/coolify-localhost bunker-qa.sh launch /home/kara/coding-hermes-boardctl (then collect). Local: act --bind on the repo, or cd repo && go test ./... (passes natively). Fix direction: re-run act with full logs, identify the failing Test assertion, decide workflow-env vs real defect.", "type": null, "created_by": "qa-foreman", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null}
 {"id": "QA-BOARDCTL-3", "title": "QA chaos-resource: go test ./... OOMs under a 3G memory cap in the ci-pass container profile (INFO - brittleness, battery 2026-10-01)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "QA foreman cycle 2026-10-01 - fresh-system CI pass + chaos on hermes4friends (cell chaos-resource). Under a 3145728KB cgroup cap the suite hits OOM ('ok ... boardctl/internal/workflowcheck' followed by FAIL on a later package). Harmless on unconstrained hosts, but the suite is not memory-flat: in any constrained CI runner or container the test run dies instead of degrading. Worth a t-scalable tag on the heaviest package or -p tuning; not a correctness defect today.", "created_at": "2026-10-01 12:26:05", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "6dc6a63edefe8952680257dc82ad03fb509139ec", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "3G-cap suite OOM fixed: (1) TestServeOversizeCap413 was materialising a 512MiB buffer (~1GiB RSS with the multipart copy) to reach a branch that refuses on ContentLength before reading — now posts a tiny body with honest oversized ContentLength-header; (2) TestVulncheck under an address-space cap (ulimit -v) could not start the govulncheck child at all — now skips loudly when RLIMIT_AS is finite (CI stays uncapped and enforces the gate). Verified: make test green under systemd-run scope MemoryMax=3145728K on this host (11 pkgs ok) x2, green uncapped, gofmt/vet clean. Tier1 guard PASS, Tier2 judge PASS (.gitreins/history/2026-10-02/62f97c91/verdict.json, id ca317865).", "complexity": null, "updated_at": "2026-10-02 02:35:00", "foreman_note": "Tick boardctl-2026-10-01-23-32-48. Repro->fix->gate-proven under cap; commit 6dc6a63 pushed origin/main.", "completed_at": "2026-10-02 02:35:00", "depends_on": [], "review_notes": "EVIDENCE /tmp/qa-20261001-boardctl.jsonl cell=chaos-resource: 'OOM under cap (expected for heavy suites, cap=3145728KB child_saw=3145728 ...): ok github.com/